{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502725-how-do-you-think-knowledge-of-the-the-spirit-realms-would-affect-vampire-society","id":1502725,"title":"How do you think knowledge of the the Spirit Realms would affect Vampire society?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-10T18:58:43-08:00","id":1502725,"title":"How do you think knowledge of the the Spirit Realms would affect Vampire society?","content":"Vampires can enter the Astral realm, Underworld, and the Spirit Wilds using certain disciplines, paths, and rituals, and can interact with the inhabitants of these realms in a similar manner. While many of these powers are difficult to obtain, there is one discipline that is quite common among the clans that allows you to travel into the spiritual realm, and that is Auspex, which at the 5th level does allow you to do just that. Now, most vampires may never get to this level, however, those who do would surely tell others of what they've experienced, and while yes, many would probably not believe what they hear at first, it would surely be supported by others who have gone through the same experience themselves.<br /> <br /> Taking into consideration the fact that 3 out of 4 schools of Anarch Sorcery include 1-2 paths that in some form allows them to deal with either spirits or wraiths, and how Anarch Sorcery seems to be quite well known among the Anarchs, it would not be a stretch to say that knowledge of the Umbra and its inhabitants should be quite widespread.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, if knowledge of the Spirit Realms became widespread, there would be a shift in priorities. Many may decide that they would much rather explore the umbra and commune with spirits and ghosts rather than involve themselves too heavily in politics and sect warfare. Some among the Anarchs and Sabbat may decide to create new Paths of Enlightenment to help themselves and their allies survive and prosper in this brand new territory, and many among the Camarilla may try to learn Thaumaturgy and Necromancy to better deal with the creatures within the Umbra.<br /> <br /> What about you?\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T19:38:23-08:00","id":1502726,"title":"","content":"I disagree. Almost all the powers of vampires deal with the real world and are useless in the umbra. They are at a disadvantage against most umbral entities. They are also unholy abominations that either anger many of these umbral entities by their very existence or attract the attention of umbral entities that would want to manipulate them. They have little information in which to navigate these strange and mysterious dimensions. Nothing in there can provide blood to them, which they need to continue to exist. And the vast majority of these entities have only tangential effects on the real world and therefore cannot offer them much help. This is a high risk, low reward situation.<br /> <br /> Rather than wanting to explore the Umbra, most vampires would probably conclude that the rewards are not worth the risks inherent in Umbral travel or neglecting their affairs in the real world. At the end of the day, a vampire needs a steady supply of blood, safety from the sun during the day, and protection from various forces that would seek to destroy her. For the vast majority of vampires, the umbra would merely be a curiosity or distraction from much more important matters.<br /> <br /> Now for those vampires truly interested in the occult, they would want to attempt some exploration, but only after their more immediate needs are met. At best, it would be a supplement to their ongoing existence and paranoid dealings with vampire politics and the Masquerade, not a replacement for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T21:03:11-08:00","id":1502729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502725-how-do-you-think-knowledge-of-the-the-spirit-realms-would-affect-vampire-society?p=1502726#post1502726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. Almost all the powers of vampires deal with the real world and are useless in the umbra. They are at a disadvantage against most umbral entities. They are also unholy abominations that either anger many of these umbral entities by their very existence or attract the attention of umbral entities that would want to manipulate them. They have little information in which to navigate these strange and mysterious dimensions. Nothing in there can provide blood to them, which they need to continue to exist. And the vast majority of these entities have only tangential effects on the real world and therefore cannot offer them much help. This is a high risk, low reward situation.<br /> <br /> Rather than wanting to explore the Umbra, most vampires would probably conclude that the rewards are not worth the risks inherent in Umbral travel or neglecting their affairs in the real world. At the end of the day, a vampire needs a steady supply of blood, safety from the sun during the day, and protection from various forces that would seek to destroy her. For the vast majority of vampires, the umbra would merely be a curiosity or distraction from much more important matters.<br /> <br /> Now for those vampires truly interested in the occult, they would want to attempt some exploration, but only after their more immediate needs are met. At best, it would be a supplement to their ongoing existence and paranoid dealings with vampire politics and the Masquerade, not a replacement for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>True many a vampire would die. But surely many would do proper research before stepping foot into the Umbra. No doubt clans like Tremere, Assamites, FoS, Tzim and anarch sorcery shchools would create rituals or new paths that would help them survive in the umbra. Perhaps the Tremere come out with the Path of Essence, a thaumathurgy path that lets you alter spirits and even feed on them, maybe one of the powers on the path allows you to even feed a spirit some vitae giving you a tool to help tame some spirits, or at least help negotiate with them. Perhaps some assamite comes up with a ritual that allows them to merge their essence with a spirit, to become a spirit canite hybrid. Maybe an anarch sorcerer comes up with a ritual that makes spirits ignore your presence.<br /> <br /> Sure many kindered will die, but if its any consolidation, at least their deaths will build the foundation for which future generations will stand on. Hopefull the future generation of kindered living in a colonized part of the umbra will remember those pioneers who came before them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T04:28:53-08:00","id":1502738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502725-how-do-you-think-knowledge-of-the-the-spirit-realms-would-affect-vampire-society?p=1502726#post1502726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. Almost all the powers of vampires deal with the real world and are useless in the umbra. They are at a disadvantage against most umbral entities. They are also unholy abominations that either anger many of these umbral entities by their very existence or attract the attention of umbral entities that would want to manipulate them. They have little information in which to navigate these strange and mysterious dimensions. Nothing in there can provide blood to them, which they need to continue to exist. And the vast majority of these entities have only tangential effects on the real world and therefore cannot offer them much help. This is a high risk, low reward situation.<br /> <br /> Rather than wanting to explore the Umbra, most vampires would probably conclude that the rewards are not worth the risks inherent in Umbral travel or neglecting their affairs in the real world. At the end of the day, a vampire needs a steady supply of blood, safety from the sun during the day, and protection from various forces that would seek to destroy her. For the vast majority of vampires, the umbra would merely be a curiosity or distraction from much more important matters.<br /> <br /> Now for those vampires truly interested in the occult, they would want to attempt some exploration, but only after their more immediate needs are met. At best, it would be a supplement to their ongoing existence and paranoid dealings with vampire politics and the Masquerade, not a replacement for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True many a vampire would die. But surely many would do proper research before stepping foot into the Umbra. No doubt clans like Tremere, Assamites, FoS, Tzim and anarch sorcery shchools would create rituals or new paths that would help them survive in the umbra. Perhaps the Tremere come out with the Path of Essence, a thaumathurgy path that lets you alter spirits and even feed on them, maybe one of the powers on the path allows you to even feed a spirit some vitae giving you a tool to help tame some spirits, or at least help negotiate with them. Perhaps some assamite comes up with a ritual that allows them to merge their essence with a spirit, to become a spirit canite hybrid. Maybe an anarch sorcerer comes up with a ritual that makes spirits ignore your presence.<br /> <br /> Sure many kindered will die, but if its any consolidation, at least their deaths will build the foundation for which future generations will stand on. Hopefull the future generation of kindered living in a colonized part of the umbra will remember those pioneers who came before them.\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T05:33:49-08:00","id":1502742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502725-how-do-you-think-knowledge-of-the-the-spirit-realms-would-affect-vampire-society#post1502725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion, if knowledge of the Spirit Realms became widespread, there would be a shift in priorities. Many may decide that they would much rather explore the umbra and commune with spirits and ghosts rather than involve themselves too heavily in politics and sect warfare. Some among the Anarchs and Sabbat may decide to create new Paths of Enlightenment to help themselves and their allies survive and prosper in this brand new territory, and many among the Camarilla may try to learn Thaumaturgy and Necromancy to better deal with the creatures within the Umbra.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the issue is that the Spirit Realms don't exactly solve vampiric problems, so much as they give alternative avenues for further problems. A single dot of Fortitude/Obfuscate/Dominate/Celerity/etc. can be the difference between surviving a random encounter, but none of the other planar powers can make the same claim.<br /> <br /> The true spirit realms are the purview of the various shape shifters, which means unless you are dealing with Banes, all the locals hate you on sight and will probably inform their local lupines about you.<br /> <br /> The underworld is tricky because the few clans that have access to necromancy tend to enslave or in some cases eat the ghosts. <br /> <br /> The way cainites are setup on a mechanical level means that just getting access to the alternative planes of existence is quite the investment. The old Kindred of the East line had the Kuei-jin more or less setup to work with the kitchen sink cosmology of the WoD from the word go. Thus, the cross-play potential and the more unified setting made sense.<br /> <br /> VtM suffers from being the flagship splat which means all the cool ideas that came later either have to be retconned into existence or left as obvious plot holes. Kind of like how all vampires are nocturnal, but only one power in one discipline allows you to see in the dark and they are all afraid of fire..... so how did they function prior to the invention of the electric lightbulb?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T09:07:01-08:00","id":1502757,"title":"","content":"Not at all. You wasting time in the spirit realm is a good opportunity for your enemies to burn your house and steal your retainers. For Tremere it's more a good opertunity for your chantry members to steal your research or stigmatize you for spending so much time away from reality. That's before we get into the whole &quot;spirit world is dangerously cray-cray&quot; stuff. <br /> <br /> Spirit thaumaturgy 4 is interesting but giving away magical artefacts that you've made and continue to have a strong connection with is a good way for rival thaumaturges to target you since they get a nice bonus when they use magic against you holding one of your artefacts .<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T09:41:18-08:00","id":1502758,"title":"","content":"No I don't see having spirit lore having much affect on vampire society and most kindred know that spirits and ghosts really hate them and for good reasons. At best all I could see is learning just enough to protect themselves against such beings and not much else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T12:00:52-08:00","id":1502765,"title":"","content":"In most vampire games I\u2019ve played and run the spirit worlds only come into play if the spirit world itself is making problems (most often the hauntings which vampires somewhat inevitably generate) or because those clans or individuals who like to have high occult scores are doing occult chicanery.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d say the majority of vampires treat the spirit world with the same philosophy as vampirism - if vampires exist, then why not ghosts? If vampirism reaffirmed their mortal faiths they\u2019ll probably use that as a framework to understand the occult world. That said, for the vast majority, it will come up very rarely if at all.<br /> <br /> For those vampires who it will come up for (Tremere, Giovanni, Blood Sorcerers, Spiritualists Mediums, Oracles, etc.) I imagine they take precautions and use the information they get as a resource in personal affairs as well as politics, which means they have a highly specialized and particular skill set. In most domains if you\u2019re having spiritual or ghost problems that need to be resolved you\u2019ll go to the nearest Tremere, Giovanni, Blood Sorcerer, or Sabbat Priest who seems to know what they\u2019re talking about. Let those specialists wrangle the occult problems in exchange for whatever barter in favors or booms is deemed appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T15:42:21-08:00","id":1502779,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist\">It's that time of the year again?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T15:56:57-08:00","id":1502783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502725-how-do-you-think-knowledge-of-the-the-spirit-realms-would-affect-vampire-society?p=1502779#post1502779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist\">It's that time of the year again?</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I feel at least a few vampires would be willing to explore at least part of the umbra. We already see something similar to this with the giovanni. It seems reasonanble that occult minded clans and gropus would create some rituals and paths that would help them better survive and even prosper in the umbra. If the giovanni can create a path that allows them to feed on ghosts, then theres no reason for it to be impossible to create a power that feeds on spirits, or even a ritual that acts as obfuscate against spirits.<br /> <br /> It doesent seem like that big of a stretch for vampires to colanize at least a small area of the umbra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 02-11-2023, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T10:10:33-08:00","id":1502849,"title":"","content":"Firstly, I do believe that there would be combination Disciplines out there that would make transversing into the Otherworlds easier and more survivable. It is hard to believe that in all of the millennia of vampire existence that there wouldn't be more exploration of such realms. Someone, somewhere would have asked questions and started exploring. Note that the Black Hand knew about the Underworld for centuries, so information on that section would be out there. The Assamites sorcerers frequently engaged in exploration of what could be Astral realms. Just a few fights with Lupines would suggest the Middle Umbra exists. Now, with all of that being said, Fifth Edition rules lack the primary Auspex power, Astral Projection, that would be the basis for much of this exploration. Even the Ceremonies for Oblivion barely mention such travel is possible. This could be due to the fact that the Otherworlds weren't planned out yet, for the other game lines for instance. However, with the de-emphasis on the spirit worlds in the current hints about Werewolf Fifth Edition, this could be intentional, and the spirit worlds are more like what they are in CoD games than they were in the original WoD, simpler and just not as important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T12:12:02-08:00","id":1502864,"title":"","content":"I do agree that it would be great if the game provided more details on how vampires could interact with the umbra because of the Astral Projection power. How would a vampire experience the Astral Plane? How could she enter the other umbra through it. What are the key points of presenting the underworld, middle umbra, astral, etc. in the context of VtM? What kind of stories can be told, encounters that have meaning, obstacles that would result, and the benefits and hazards that could result if a vampire explores things? What were the other entities that a vampire could encounter and on what kind of frequency so an ST had a guide to help him navigate this?<br /> <br /> Even though this power existed prior to the other game lines, we should have gotten some kind of sourcebook - or a significant section in the STs Handbook - on this by the Revised era. Reconcile what the other game lines did, and interpret them so it is appropriate for VtM. Instead, all we got was &quot;the astral plane is kind of like all the others combined, but completely different&quot; which was not very helpful. Instead, Astral Project was just another spy power instead of being something that could really add to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T13:00:40-08:00","id":1502869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502725-how-do-you-think-knowledge-of-the-the-spirit-realms-would-affect-vampire-society?p=1502742#post1502742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Part of the issue is that the Spirit Realms don't exactly solve vampiric problems, so much as they give alternative avenues for further problems. A single dot of Fortitude/Obfuscate/Dominate/Celerity/etc. can be the difference between surviving a random encounter, but none of the other planar powers can make the same claim.<br /> <br /> The true spirit realms are the purview of the various shape shifters, which means unless you are dealing with Banes, all the locals hate you on sight and will probably inform their local lupines about you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Banes also hate you, though, and will tell the local BSDs. Or just take it into their own hands to deal with you as appropriate, though they'll likely also keep their distance because vampires are spirit roach motels to everything but blood banes and psychomachiae. And that's when vampires get rudely introduced to the concept of &quot;Fortitude doesn't provide enough soak to survive even a scraggling's gnashing on you&quot;, unless you happen to be playing in a Mage rather than Werewolf crossover. Sometimes, you might meet one willing to cut a deal, of course, but vampires don't speak spirit, so that limits the pool of potential candidates for intrigue, and in any case, caveat emptor has never been truer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The underworld is tricky because the few clans that have access to necromancy tend to enslave or in some cases eat the ghosts.<br /> <br /> The way cainites are setup on a mechanical level means that just getting access to the alternative planes of existence is quite the investment. The old Kindred of the East line had the Kuei-jin more or less setup to work with the kitchen sink cosmology of the WoD from the word go. Thus, the cross-play potential and the more unified setting made sense.<br /> <br /> VtM suffers from being the flagship splat which means all the cool ideas that came later either have to be retconned into existence or left as obvious plot holes. Kind of like how all vampires are nocturnal, but only one power in one discipline allows you to see in the dark and they are all afraid of fire..... so how did they function prior to the invention of the electric lightbulb? </div> </div> </div>Maybe before electricity they had Hollywood-style vein-o-vision, and then just forgot that they could do that? (^VVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T08:49:05-08:00","id":1502933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502725-how-do-you-think-knowledge-of-the-the-spirit-realms-would-affect-vampire-society?p=1502869#post1502869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Banes also hate you, though</div> </div> </div> </div>I find the idea that all spirits hate vampires a little hard to believe. A good chunk of spirits represent concepts and a good chunk of those are going to represent concepts entirely agreeable to vampire existence. Especially when Vampires are probably going to be looking in their backyards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 02-13-2023, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T09:08:39-08:00","id":1503145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502725-how-do-you-think-knowledge-of-the-the-spirit-realms-would-affect-vampire-society?p=1502933#post1502933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find the idea that all spirits hate vampires a little hard to believe. A good chunk of spirits represent concepts and a good chunk of those are going to represent concepts entirely agreeable to vampire existence. Especially when Vampires are probably going to be looking in their backyards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but much as with vampires themselves, what's okay with vampires existing doesn't necessarily not hate other vampires. Also, a lot of banes aren't really all that bright, so their method of expressing that might be... unsophisticated. Not trying to hook them into a very terrible occult deal or getting them to just straight up do what the bane wants, bane has no time for that. Bane smash!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T20:16:14-08:00","id":1503298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502725-how-do-you-think-knowledge-of-the-the-spirit-realms-would-affect-vampire-society?p=1502726#post1502726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. Almost all the powers of vampires deal with the real world and are useless in the umbra. . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly due to the fact each OWoD game-system was stand-alone and there were difficulties in mixing the games. The Spirit-world described in V:tPG etc. was different than the spirit-world described in WW:tA. I found it easier just to convert, say, werewolves, into a V:tM with Vampire disciplines. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T10:56:01-08:00","id":1503333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502725-how-do-you-think-knowledge-of-the-the-spirit-realms-would-affect-vampire-society#post1502725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires can enter the Astral realm, Underworld, and the Spirit Wilds using certain disciplines, paths, and rituals, and can interact with the inhabitants of these realms in a similar manner. While many of these powers are difficult to obtain, there is one discipline that is quite common among the clans that allows you to travel into the spiritual realm, and that is Auspex, which at the 5th level does allow you to do just that. Now, most vampires may never get to this level, however, those who do would surely tell others of what they've experienced, and while yes, many would probably not believe what they hear at first, it would surely be supported by others who have gone through the same experience themselves.<br /> <br /> Taking into consideration the fact that 3 out of 4 schools of Anarch Sorcery include 1-2 paths that in some form allows them to deal with either spirits or wraiths, and how Anarch Sorcery seems to be quite well known among the Anarchs, it would not be a stretch to say that knowledge of the Umbra and its inhabitants should be quite widespread.<br /> <br /> In my opinion, if knowledge of the Spirit Realms became widespread, there would be a shift in priorities. Many may decide that they would much rather explore the umbra and commune with spirits and ghosts rather than involve themselves too heavily in politics and sect warfare. Some among the Anarchs and Sabbat may decide to create new Paths of Enlightenment to help themselves and their allies survive and prosper in this brand new territory, and many among the Camarilla may try to learn Thaumaturgy and Necromancy to better deal with the creatures within the Umbra.<br /> <br /> What about you?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It has to be noted that the supernatural persons (be it Wraiths, urban Spirits, nature Animas, or other kinds and types of persons and beings dwelling in various ephemeral and magical worlds, environments, realms, and also levels) in various Umbras could react to such interest and actions with a wide variety of choices, ways, and responses. It might not be that easy, repeatable, or predictable for a particular Vampiress (or a group of Vampires) to develop her knowledge and method related to various otherwordly and special domains or environments.<br /> <br /> Mages - be it Mystics or Technocrats - could also change or influence the outcomes and result. Certainly the knowledge, abilities, items, trinkets, and skills that the Magi have could be interesting and helpful under a positive and careful approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 02-17-2023, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T06:13:08-08:00","id":1503443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502725-how-do-you-think-knowledge-of-the-the-spirit-realms-would-affect-vampire-society?p=1503333#post1503333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It has to be noted that the supernatural persons (be it Wraiths, urban Spirits, nature Animas, or other kinds and types of persons and beings dwelling in various ephemeral and magical worlds, environments, realms, and also levels) in various Umbras could react to such interest and actions with a wide variety of choices, ways, and responses. It might not be that easy, repeatable, or predictable for a particular Vampiress (or a group of Vampires) to develop her knowledge and method related to various otherwordly and special domains or environments.<br /> <br /> Mages - be it Mystics or Technocrats - could also change or influence the outcomes and result. Certainly the knowledge, abilities, items, trinkets, and skills that the Magi have could be interesting and helpful under a positive and careful approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe this is where the nature of blood magic, specifically thaumathurgy, would be extremely helpful. Blood magic itself is a constantly evolving discipline that can adapt to almost any circumstance, we see an example of this with the Path of Technomancy, a tremere made thuamathurgy path. Who is to say the Tremere arent working on a path or ritual that would help them to create chantrys in the Umbra, or ones that allow you to merge with a spirit, maybe even one that allows you to feed on spirits? While it may not be easy, almost nothing is when it comes to gaining power in Vampire society. With the right paths and rituals it would surely help in gaining proper knwledge of the Umbra and its inhabitants.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 02-19-2023, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T15:24:25-08:00","id":1503495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502725-how-do-you-think-knowledge-of-the-the-spirit-realms-would-affect-vampire-society?p=1503333#post1503333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It has to be noted that the supernatural persons (be it Wraiths, urban Spirits, nature Animas, or other kinds and types of persons and beings dwelling in various ephemeral and magical worlds, environments, realms, and also levels) in various Umbras could react to such interest and actions with a wide variety of choices, ways, and responses. It might not be that easy, repeatable, or predictable for a particular Vampiress (or a group of Vampires) to develop her knowledge and method related to various otherwordly and special domains or environments.<br /> <br /> Mages - be it Mystics or Technocrats - could also change or influence the outcomes and result. Certainly the knowledge, abilities, items, trinkets, and skills that the Magi have could be interesting and helpful under a positive and careful approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe this is where the nature of blood magic, specifically thaumathurgy, would be extremely helpful. Blood magic itself is a constantly evolving discipline that can adapt to almost any circumstance, we see an example of this with the Path of Technomancy, a tremere made thuamathurgy path. Who is to say the Tremere arent working on a path or ritual that would help them to create chantrys in the Umbra, or ones that allow you to merge with a spirit, maybe even one that allows you to feed on spirits? While it may not be easy, almost nothing is when it comes to gaining power in Vampire society. With the right paths and rituals it would surely help in gaining proper knwledge of the Umbra and its inhabitants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T16:35:12-08:00","id":1503497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502725-how-do-you-think-knowledge-of-the-the-spirit-realms-would-affect-vampire-society?p=1502933#post1502933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find the idea that all spirits hate vampires a little hard to believe. A good chunk of spirits represent concepts and a good chunk of those are going to represent concepts entirely agreeable to vampire existence. Especially when Vampires are probably going to be looking in their backyards.</div> </div> </div> </div>If anything, Banes should LOVE vampires. They're not really able to gain purchase in one, which is a mood killer. But some Banes love being around vampires, because they're often doing very Wyrmish things, just as a consequence of what many vampires are like.<br /> <br /> By extension, some vampires may have bad things happen around them, from congregating Banes. Gaining a reputation as a walking jinx, or as a harbinger of doom and corruption. (Maybe this is where certain Flaws come from?)<br /> <br /> Imagine a coterie is investigating a powerful vampire, only for those with Auspex turning on aura vision, and just seeing their target wreathed in unclean spirits. Swarming around them, like the vampire is the eye of the storm. Can Auspex aura reading even see Banes? Maybe in this case, it's impossible not to, with how thick they are.<br /> <br /> It would certainly be a disturbing revelation, especially for PCs who know absolutely nothing about the occult. They don't know what this is, just that it's clear something is VERY wrong with the NPC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T10:12:09-08:00","id":1503821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502725-how-do-you-think-knowledge-of-the-the-spirit-realms-would-affect-vampire-society?p=1503443#post1503443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe this is where the nature of blood magic, specifically thaumathurgy, would be extremely helpful. Blood magic itself is a constantly evolving discipline that can adapt to almost any circumstance, we see an example of this with the Path of Technomancy, a tremere made thuamathurgy path. Who is to say the Tremere arent working on a path or ritual that would help them to create chantrys in the Umbra, or ones that allow you to merge with a spirit, maybe even one that allows you to feed on spirits? While it may not be easy, almost nothing is when it comes to gaining power in Vampire society. With the right paths and rituals it would surely help in gaining proper knwledge of the Umbra and its inhabitants.</div> </div> </div> </div>The natural abilities of the Kindred (and also of Ghouls and Revenants) - boosting Attributes, better senses, regeneration, and other qualities - can also be useful in regard ot interaction with various animas and spirits, and also when dealing with the exploration of umbral and otherwordly places. This might be especially visible, nice, and helpful when a group, organisation, or a team of various different supernatural persons would be working together in regard to these interests, ideas, and matters to increase their reliabiltiy and chances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-24T10:47:37-08:00","id":1503827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502725-how-do-you-think-knowledge-of-the-the-spirit-realms-would-affect-vampire-society?p=1502779#post1502779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487803-why-are-vampires-so-calm-with-the-fact-that-spirits-exist\">It's that time of the year again?</a></div> </div> </div> </div>No it came earlier this year!\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"